{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/157","id":4744267966,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTEdTLM8AAAABGsfIvg","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/157","diff_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/157.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/157.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/157","number":157,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prove finite constrained-loss criterion for Orabona Chapter 2","user":{"login":"jicheng9617","id":74550583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTUwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74550583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617","html_url":"https://github.com/jicheng9617","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Orabona Chapter 2 says that adding the extended indicator forces any finite-loss prediction or comparator into the feasible set. This package proves the exact finite-real-witness iff: feasibility **and finite original loss**. A separate effective-domain intersection theorem retains global noBottom, with a public counterexample showing why that premise cannot be dropped. Both use ordinary EReal addition and the existing shared definitions, root and declaration registry.\n\nThe iff is an explicit refinement of the unnumbered source necessity, and arbitrary carriers generalize its Euclidean instance; neither endpoint is attributed as a new numbered source theorem. Two genuine proofs, eight public canaries and two source-qualified Book notes close this precise missing consequence. Chapter 2 and the Chapters 1–16 Goal remain incomplete.\n\nStacked on OPEN draft #156, exact base `f6daaa68927398df9fd8b756f3ac2dd28247c1e7`. This is not direct main integration: the main-relative contributor audit still reports sixteen legacy production-contract gaps.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Shared root: 9088 jobs; Tests: 9230 jobs; full harness: 466 tests, 7 existing skips.\n- Two unchanged frozen headers/native guards; ten named axiom audits use only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.\n- Fresh scoped compiled-environment graph: two nodes, 121 direct edges; not a full graph or canary export.\n- Exact stacked contributor gate: five production paths, one contract. Scoped code/JSON/docs whitespace passes; full whitespace check fails on preserved raw logs.\n- Clean lean-verified site source `8acd4a19291cf0b0e62e31c8baf3565707a510e7`; two canonical nodes and all 10804 inherited IDs/URLs verified. Actual isolated browser first viewport inspected.\n- Distinct automated source-blind reconstruction, contract/body/final source-reader reviews and immutable binding audit. No human or external review is claimed.\n\nEvidence: `runs/online-finite-loss-20261005/accepted-decision-v1.json`, `native-acceptance-overlay-v2.json`, `accepted-binding-audit-v1.json`, `final-reader-receipt-v1.json`, contracts under `docs/contracts/online-finite-loss-v1`. Failed probe/canary/parser/harness/schema/site/native-attempt gates and exact originals remain versioned with their actual repairs; no mathematical terminal was weakened. Generated canonical `_site`, frozen anonymous sources and global SGB frontier were not edited.\n","created_at